<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Warmians</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1274 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Prussian people of Warmia, around the Vistula Lagoon, whose land became the Prince-Bishopric of Warmia after the Teutonic conquest.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Warmians lived in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-warmia">Warmia</a>, south-east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula-lagoon">Vistula Lagoon</a> in today's northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. They were one of the Prussian peoples recorded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-of-dusburg">Peter of Dusburg</a>, with settlements along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pasleka">Pasłęka</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyna">Łyna</a> rivers.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Warmian society was led by nobles who held hillforts and controlled farming land, and its people kept the Prussian religion. The coast linked them to Baltic trade, including amber.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> invaded in 1239, founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balga-castle">Balga</a> castle, and soon dominated <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-warmia">Warmia</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-prussian-uprising">Great Prussian Uprising</a> the Warmians fought under their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glappe">Glappe</a>, who was captured and hanged at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konigsberg">Königsberg</a>. By 1274 they were subdued, and their land became the Bishopric of Warmia, a prince-bishopric that passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in 1466.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/warmians.jpg" alt="Warmians" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: JakaśKreatywnaNazwa123 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Warmia_plemienna_na_mapie_adm._Polski_i_Rosji.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1274 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Glappe</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Baltic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Prussian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Warmia (Prussian land), Wormditten</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1037&amp;focus=warmians" aria-label="Warmians on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5113 368 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Warmians lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5451 561h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5433 624h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5433 624h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Poland. <a href="/atlas?year=1037&amp;focus=warmians">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

